[Run MNIST]($link.page('zml/quickstart').attrs('zml-run-mnist'))
Build with Bazel and classify a handwritten digit.

# [Follow the model lifecycle]($heading.id('follow-the-model-lifecycle'))

```=html
<figure class="execution-diagram" aria-label="ZML model execution">
  <div class="execution-paths">
    <span class="execution-path-title" id="compile-model-code">Compile model code</span>
    <ol class="execution-path" role="list" aria-labelledby="compile-model-code">
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Zig model code</strong>
        <span><code>forward</code> and symbolic tensor shapes and types</span>
        <a class="execution-guide" href="first-model/">Write your first ZML model</a>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Compile for the selected backend</strong>
        <span>Trace to StableHLO and compile through PJRT</span>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-artifact">Executable</li>
    </ol>
    <span class="execution-path-title" id="prepare-runtime-data">Prepare runtime data</span>
    <ol class="execution-path" role="list" aria-labelledby="prepare-runtime-data">
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Model weights and inputs</strong>
        <span>Weight values from Safetensors and input data</span>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-node">
        <strong>Fill backend buffers</strong>
        <span>Load weights and transfer inputs to the selected backend</span>
        <a class="execution-guide" href="checkpoints/">Load model weights</a>
      </li>
      <li class="execution-artifact">Device buffers</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="execution-run">
    <strong>Run on the selected backend</strong>
    <span>Call the executable with the weight and input buffers to produce output tensors.</span>
    <a class="execution-guide" href="sharding/">Run ZML across devices</a>
  </div>
  <figcaption>Safetensors metadata can supply weight shapes and data types for the symbolic tensors used during compilation.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

Read [ZML concepts]($link.page('zml/concepts')) for tensors, shapes, and dimension tags.
Use the [Tensor reference]($link.page('zml/api/tensor')) to look up model operations
and the [Exe reference]($link.page('zml/api/exe')) for calls that run a compiled model.
See [Build and run with Bazel]($link.page('zml/build-and-run')) for accelerator
flags, LLM examples, and packaging.

See [LLMD on ZML]($link.page('llmd/architecture')) for how the serving engine uses
these executables and buffers to run inference requests.

ZML uses Zig, MLIR, and Bazel. The [upstream ZML repository](https://github.com/zml/zml)
contains examples and framework documentation. Record the source revision and
environment to reproduce your build.

# [Choose the server path when appropriate]($heading.id('choose-the-server-path-when-appropriate'))

For an application that calls a model over HTTP, continue to
[LLMD]($link.page('llmd')). For service management, continue to
[Operations]($link.page('operations')).
